Alexis wrote:
> I'm trying to think of a good way to allow people to easily access / set
> this info without spoiling people.

In the end, if people want to be spoiled, there are easy ways to do
this. You could just save up a lot of your own bones files, and
constantly re-deploy them. A more advanced user could just hack source
to make the game easier.

Nethack on one's own computer is for your own fun. If you want to hack
it up, or cheat in some way (depending on one's definition of cheat),
then you can do so. Maybe the game is still fun for someone that way.
Maybe not.

I think comments on bones files might be really fun as a story telling
mechanism. If people want to abuse this, they certainly can, but I
probably wouldn't try to put any artificial restriction on some service
to a game that is all open anyway. If someone wants to be forced into
proper behavior, then servers like nethack.alt.org, or the devnull
tourney, are setup to make a best attempt to maintain a consistent
environment for "on the record" play.

For a user that wants to stay "clean" in a game, it would probably be
best not to read bones files comments until after the game is over, if
they are available through a service such as you describe.

Anyway, just a different perspective.

